<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Complutum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Complutum was a Roman city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>, on the site of modern Alcalá de Henares near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a>, which grew from a settlement of the Carpetani. It flourished in the imperial period, with a forum and rich houses with mosaics. The martyrdom of the boys Justus and Pastor there around 304 made it a Christian centre, around which the later town grew.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/complutum.jpg" alt="Complutum" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rowanwindwhistler · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mosaico_de_Baco_(Alcal%C3%A1_de_Henares).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
